message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
title: "PASV — Possibility-Adjusted Shot Value: A Per-Shot Theory of Possibility Cost in NBA Possession Value"
abstract: >-
  PASV (Possibility-Adjusted Shot Value) is a per-shot signed scalar that grades each
  NBA shot decision against the continuation value of the alternatives the shot
  forecloses: PASV = xPTS(shot) − V*(s*). It unifies Skinner's (2012) MDP-cutoff and
  Cervone et al.'s (2014) Expected Possession Value into a single, interpretable,
  per-shot decision grade, accompanied by the closed-form Holding-Math Theorem and the
  Option Preservation Coefficient (OPC). Companion code, data, and pre-registration for
  the MIT Sloan Sports Analytics Conference 2027 submission.
type: software
